# Do not reintroduce these false positives

Full log: [docs/AUDIT.md](docs/AUDIT.md).

## Queue worker hourly mail (2026-09-14)

`queue:work --max-time=3600` exits cleanly every hour; Docker restarts it. Not a crash.

- Mail `restart_loop` only for a real loop (2 polls still restarting, or 3 restarts in 10 min).
- Do not mail `restart_count` for expected recyclers on a single recycle.
- Do not delete `--max-time` from the panel queue command to silence alerts.

## Log scan checkpoint, dashboard loop, URL traceback (2026-09-14)

- Checkpoint the last Docker log **timestamp**. Do not hash the whole tail window
  (a new info line would re-mail old errors).
- Do not log-scan `vps_dashboard` (mail/SMTP failures become more mail).
- Strip HTTP request targets / JSON `uri` before severity tokens (`/.env-traceback`
  is not a traceback). Keep ignoring hashed Vite `*-error-*.js` assets.

## Postgres `pg_isready` must pass `-d $DB` (2026-09-14)

Healthcheck is `pg_isready -U ${DB_USERNAME:-laravel} -d ${DB_DATABASE:-laravel}`.
Without `-d`, a user like `app_user` probes a database named `app_user` while the
real DB is `app_db`, logging `FATAL` every 5s with health still green.

## Exit 137 is not OOM (2026-09-14)

OOM only when Docker sets `OOMKilled`. Compose recreate / stop-timeout SIGKILL
is exit 137 without that flag — treat it like 143, not “Ran out of memory”.

## Log scan vs Vite assets (2026-09-08)

Do not substring-match `error` in hashed frontend asset names. Keep `log_match.py`.
